+# ApertureCoin fork of the SRI applications
+
+This fork of [stratum-mining/sv2-apps](https://github.com/stratum-mining/sv2-apps)
+runs the Stratum V2 reference pool, JD server, JD client, translator and CPU
+mining device against [ApertureCoin](https://github.com/IlumCI/Aperturecoin)
+(ticker SCIENCE). The Stratum V2 protocol is unchanged. Only the parts that
+depend on the chain differ:
+
+| Area | Upstream | This fork |
+|---|---|---|
+| Share and block proof of work | `SHA256d(header)` | ApertureMatMul v1: `BLAKE3(header \|\| BLAKE3(A·B))`, int8 n×n matrices from `BLAKE3-XOF("ApertureMatMul/v1" \|\| header)` |
+| Block identifier (`BlockFound`, prev hash) | `SHA256d(header)` | unchanged: `SHA256d(header)` |
+| Payout addresses in `addr()` and user identities | Bitcoin | ApertureCoin: `sci1`/`tsci1`/`rsci1` (bech32/bech32m), base58 versions 23/83 (main) and 111/196/58 (test, regtest) |
+| Template source | Bitcoin Core IPC or sv2-tp | ApertureCoin's sv2-tp (`contrib/sv2-tp` in the ApertureCoin repository) |
+| ApertureMatMul v2 (useful work) | none | extension `0x4150`: forward pass per template, ticket shares, panel verification (below) |
+
+The template's coinbase outputs are carried into every job unchanged. These
+are the 1.5% development-fund output, the witness commitment and, once
+ApertureMatMul v2 is active, the embedding results.
+
+## Layout
+
+- `aperture/aperture-pow/`: `aperture_pow` crate. It is a bit-exact port of
+  the node's `src/crypto/matmulpow.cpp`, and its tests use the node's test
+  vectors.
+- `aperture/stratum-patches/channels-sv2/`: `channels_sv2` from
+  stratum-mining/stratum at the commit pinned in `Cargo.lock`. Share
+  validation for standard and extended channels, server and client, uses
+  `channels_sv2::aperture::pow_block_hash`. The root `Cargo.toml` swaps it in
+  with `[patch."https://github.com/stratum-mining/stratum"]`, so no other
+  upstream crate is forked.
+- `stratum-apps/src/config_helpers/coinbase_output/aperture.rs`: ApertureCoin
+  address decoding.
+- `miner-apps/translator/src/lib/utils.rs`: SV1 share validation.
+- `aperture/aperture-sv1-miner/`: `aperture-sv1-miner`, a multithreaded
+  Stratum V1 CPU miner for ApertureMatMul. It is the SV1 client for the
+  translator:
+  `aperture-sv1-miner --url <tproxy>:34255 --user <name> --threads N [--dim 32]`.
+- `integration-tests/lib/mining_device/mod.rs`: the CPU mining device hashes
+  ApertureMatMul. The SHA256d midstate fast path is disabled.
+- `aperture/config-examples/`: pool and translator configurations.
+
+## Matrix dimension
+
+ApertureMatMul uses n = 512 on mainnet and testnet and n = 32 on regtest.
+Every role must use the node's value:
+
+- pool: `aperture_pow_dim` in the TOML config;
+- every role, the pool included when the key is absent: `APERTURE_POW_DIM=<n>`,
+  or `APERTURE_NETWORK=main|test|regtest`. With neither set, n defaults to 512.
+
+## Build and test
+
+```sh
+export APERTURE_SRC=<path to the ApertureCoin source tree>   # consensus C++ for aperture_pouw
+cargo build --release -p pool_sv2 -p jd_server_sv2 -p jd_client_sv2 -p translator_sv2 \
+    -p aperture_sv1_miner -p aperture_pouw_miner --bins
+cargo build --release -p integration_tests_sv2 --bin mining_device
+cargo test --release -p aperture_pow -p aperture_pouw -p aperture_sv1_miner -p channels_sv2 -p stratum-apps --all-features
+```
+
+The end-to-end test lives in the ApertureCoin repository. It runs apertured
+(regtest, dev fund enforced), sv2-tp, this pool and this mining device. It
+checks that the pooled blocks are accepted and pay the pool through an
+`rsci1` address, and that they keep the dev-fund output. It also checks that
+every accepted share is the ApertureMatMul hash of the block header.
+A second phase covers Stratum V1:
+`aperture-sv1-miner` -> translator -> pool. The translator accepts shares
+whose SHA256d misses the share target, so it is validating ApertureMatMul.
+
+```sh
+SV2TP=<sv2-tp> SRI_POOL=target/release/pool_sv2 \
+SRI_MINING_DEVICE=target/release/mining_device \
+SRI_TRANSLATOR=target/release/translator_sv2 \
+APERTURE_SV1_MINER=target/release/aperture-sv1-miner \
+    <aperturecoin>/test/functional/feature_sri_pool.py
+```
+
+Translator config for ApertureCoin: the upstream examples work unchanged.
+Set `APERTURE_POW_DIM` (or `APERTURE_NETWORK`) in the translator's
+environment on regtest, and size `min_individual_miner_hashrate` to
+ApertureMatMul CPU rates. A CPU core does about 50k H/s at n = 32; at
+n = 512 it is far lower.
+
+## ApertureMatMul v2 pooling (proof of useful work)
+
+Under v2, a share is a *ticket*: one r×r×r tile of the noisy forward-pass
+matmuls of the protocol model, run over the template's embedding requests
+(ApertureCoin `doc/pouw-v2.md`). Pooling uses the Stratum V2 extension
+`0x4150`:
+
+| Message | Direction | Content |
+|---|---|---|
+| UsefulWorkTemplate (0x01) | sv2-tp → pool | template_id, batch_root, model_id, rank, requests |
+| SetUsefulWork (0x03, channel message) | pool → miner | channel_id, job_id, batch_root, model_id, rank, requests; sent before each v2 NewMiningJob |
+| SubmitSharesStandard + TLV (0x4150, 0x01) | miner → pool | op, tile_i, tile_j, span_s, r×r activation panel |
+| SubmitUsefulWorkSolution (0x02) | pool → sv2-tp | version, time, nonce, ticket, panel, coinbase |
+
+The miner negotiates `0x4150` with RequestExtensions. The pool adds it to its
+supported extensions automatically once a protocol model is configured.
+
+How the pool handles a v2 template:
+
+1. The pool holds a v2 NewTemplate until its UsefulWorkTemplate arrives. It
+   then runs the protocol model over the batch once, and only after that
+   releases the template to the channel manager. Miners are therefore never
+   given a job whose batch they cannot know.
+2. `channels_sv2` judges a v2 job's share by the ticket hash
+   (`validate_share_with_ticket`). The pool registers the verifier. Upstream
+   share accounting, duplicate detection, vardiff and `BlockFound` are
+   unchanged.
+3. The verifier:
+   - checks the ticket hash with the node's consensus code (`TicketPoW`);
+   - with `aperture_verify_panels` (the default), also requires the panel to
+     equal the pool's own forward-pass activations.
+
+   Consensus does not require the second check, because KW hardness holds for
+   any A. As pool policy it makes every pooled share provably work on the real
+   inference.
+4. A share that meets the network target goes to sv2-tp as
+   SubmitUsefulWorkSolution. sv2-tp rebuilds the block with the v2 header
+   extension, and the embedding results are already in the template's
+   coinbase outputs.
+
+Code:
+
+- `aperture/aperture-pouw/`: `aperture_pouw` crate.
+  - Bindings to the node's consensus C++: the protocol model (`.apm`), the
+    integer forward pass, `Seed`/`TicketPoW` and the ticket-search kernels
+    (AVX-512 VNNI where available).
+  - It is compiled from the ApertureCoin tree named by `APERTURE_SRC`, so the
+    pool and the miner run the node's code, not a second implementation.
+  - `wire.rs` holds the message formats.
+- `aperture/aperture-pouw-miner/`: `aperture-pouw-miner`, a standard-channel
+  SV2 miner for v2 (and v1) jobs.
+- Pool:
+  - `pool-apps/pool/src/lib/aperture.rs`: model, per-template forward passes,
+    verifier, extension frames;
+  - hooks in the template receiver, downstream and share handlers.
+- `aperture/stratum-patches/channels-sv2/src/aperture.rs`:
+  `share_pow_hash` and the verifier hook.
+
+Pool configuration:
+
+```toml
+aperture_protocol_model = "/path/to/model.apm"   # the node's -protocolmodel file
+# aperture_tiny_model = 1                        # regtest tiny model instead
+# aperture_verify_panels = true                  # default
+```
+
+Miner:
+
+```sh
+aperture-pouw-miner --pool <host>:34254 --pool-key <pool authority key> --user <identity> \
+    --protocolmodel /path/to/model.apm [--threads N]
+# regtest: --tinymodel 1 --rank 8
+```
+
+Test: `test/functional/feature_sri_pool_pouw.py` in the ApertureCoin
+repository. It runs apertured, sv2-tp, this pool and `aperture-pouw-miner`
+on regtest and checks the following:
+
+- the pooled v2 blocks are accepted;
+- they pay the pool and keep the dev fund;
+- they serve the embedding requests bit-identically to the node's model;
+- their tickets are shares the pool accepted;
+- a miner submitting panels that are not the forward pass is rejected with
+  `useful-work-panel-mismatch`.
+
+Building now needs `APERTURE_SRC`:
+
+```sh
+APERTURE_SRC=<aperturecoin> cargo build --release -p pool_sv2 -p aperture_pouw_miner ...
+```
+
+## Not yet covered
+
+- v2 through the translator is not possible: Stratum V1 has no field for the
+  ticket panel. SV1 miners mine v1 only.
+- v2 through Job Declaration (JD client/server): custom jobs carry no batch,
+  so the JDS would have to run the forward pass of the declared batch. Not
+  implemented.
+- Extended channels verify v2 tickets (the same hook), but the pool sends
+  SetUsefulWork only for standard-channel and extended-channel jobs, not for
+  group-channel jobs. v2 miners therefore set REQUIRES_STANDARD_JOBS.
